/how-to/choose-a-masking-strategy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/choose-a-masking-strategy#by-what-you-need","content":"`code_set`"},"222":{"id":"/docs/how-to/choose-a-masking-strategy-42","page_id":"/docs/how-to/choose-a-masking-strategy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/choose-a-masking-strategy#by-what-you-need","content":"code\\_set"},"223":{"id":"/docs/how-to/choose-a-masking-strategy-43","page_id":"/docs/how-to/choose-a-masking-strategy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/choose-a-masking-strategy#by-what-you-need","content":"The same value for everyone in a group"},"224":{"id":"/docs/how-to/choose-a-masking-strategy-44","page_id":"/docs/how-to/choose-a-masking-strategy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/choose-a-masking-strategy#by-what-you-need","content":"`group_key`"},"225":{"id":"/docs/how-to/choose-a-masking-strategy-45","page_id":"/docs/how-to/choose-a-masking-strategy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/choose-a-masking-strategy#by-what-you-need","content":"group\\_key"},"226":{"id":"/docs/how-to/choose-a-masking-strategy-46","page_id":"/docs/how-to/choose-a-masking-strategy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/choose-a-masking-strategy#by-what-you-need","content":"Correlated columns kept consistent"},"227":{"id":"/docs/how-to/choose-a-masking-strategy-47","page_id":"/docs/how-to/choose-a-masking-strategy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/choose-a-masking-strategy#by-what-you-need","content":"`joint_mask`"},"228":{"id":"/docs/how-to/choose-a-masking-strategy-48","page_id":"/docs/how-to/choose-a-masking-strategy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/choose-a-masking-strategy#by-what-you-need","content":"joint\\_mask"},"229":{"id":"/docs/how-to/choose-a-masking-strategy-49","page_id":"/docs/how-to/choose-a-masking-strategy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/choose-a-masking-strategy#keyed-vs-one-way","content":"A **keyed** strategy (`hash`, `fpe`, `date_shift`, and others) maps the same input\nto the same output within a `namespace`, so joins survive and the column stays\nconsistent across tables. A **one-way** strategy (`redact`, `faker` without a\nvault) cannot be reversed. If you need to reverse later, see\nUnmask data."},"230":{"id":"/docs/how-to/choose-a-masking-strategy-50","page_id":"/docs/how-to/choose-a-masking-strategy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/choose-a-masking-strategy#keyed-vs-one-way","content":"For the full catalog grouped by kind, see the strategy\nreference."},"231":{"id":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data","page_id":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data","type":"page","content":"Generate synthetic data","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Guides","Build safer test datasets"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data"},"232":{"id":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data-0","page_id":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data","content":"Build a synthetic table from a column spec, then fit a real table's shape and sample from it instead."},"233":{"id":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data-1","page_id":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data#1-generate-from-a-column-spec","content":"1\\. Generate from a column spec"},"234":{"id":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data-2","page_id":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data#2-fit-a-real-tables-shape","content":"2\\. Fit a real table's shape"},"235":{"id":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data-3","page_id":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data#3-sample-from-the-snapshot","content":"3\\. Sample from the snapshot"},"236":{"id":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data-4","page_id":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data#next","content":"Next"},"237":{"id":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data-5","page_id":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data","content":"Generation needs no input file: it builds rows from a column spec you write\nby hand, or from a distribution snapshot fitted off a real table. This\nrecipe covers both, run end to end against `decoy` CLI 0.1.0."},"238":{"id":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data-6","page_id":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data#1-generate-from-a-column-spec","content":"`gen_pipeline.yaml`:"},"239":{"id":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data-7","page_id":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data#1-generate-from-a-column-spec","content":"`sources: {}` because there is nothing to read; `row_count` on the table\nsays how many rows to produce. Run it with `--mode generate`:"},"240":{"id":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data-8","page_id":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data#1-generate-from-a-column-spec","content":"1000 rows plus the header. Other `generate_columns` types: `reference`\n(mint-a-pool foreign key), `formula`/`derived` (compute from sibling\ncolumns), and `distribution` (draw from an inline snapshot). See the\nCLI reference `run` entry for the full list."},"241":{"id":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data-9","page_id":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data#2-fit-a-real-tables-shape","content":"Hand-written columns work for structural test data, but they will not\nresemble your production distribution. `decoy fit` reads a real CSV and\nwrites a `distribution-snapshot/v1` artifact: numeric histograms and\nquantiles, categorical top-k counts, datetime year bins."},"242":{"id":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data-10","page_id":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data#3-sample-from-the-snapshot","content":"A `type: statistical` generate column reads that snapshot and samples a\ncolumn shaped like the fitted one, instead of a hand-picked distribution:"},"243":{"id":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data-11","page_id":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data#3-sample-from-the-snapshot","content":"200 values drawn from the fitted `customer_id` histogram's bins, not copied\nrow-for-row from the source. With a dense 50-value source range some drawn\nvalues will coincide with a real one by chance; the numeric snapshot itself\nnever stores individual source rows, only bin edges and counts. A\n`categorical` snapshot column needs one more\nopt-in: `allow_real_categories: true` on the column, because a categorical\nsnapshot's `top_values` are real values from the source frame (its numeric\nbin edges and counts are not). `condition_on` needs a joint captured at fit\ntime with `decoy fit --joint colA,colB`."},"244":{"id":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data-12","page_id":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data#next","content":"Checking how close a generated or masked output tracks the source shape:\n`decoy validate distribution`, covered in\nuse Decoy in CI."},"245":{"id":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data-13","page_id":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/generate-synthetic-data#next","content":"A differentially private fit (`decoy fit --epsilon`) adds Laplace noise to\nevery snapshot count instead of exact quantiles; see the\nCLI reference `fit` entry."},"246":{"id":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories","page_id":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories","type":"page","content":"Handle high-cardinality categorical data","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Guides","Handle specialized data"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories"},"247":{"id":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories-0","page_id":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories","content":"Generate and preserve columns with thousands of distinct categories like diagnosis codes or SKUs."},"248":{"id":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories-1","page_id":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories#the-problem-high-cardinality","content":"The problem: high cardinality"},"249":{"id":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories-2","page_id":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories#opt-in-with-high_cardinality-true","content":"Opt in with high_cardinality: true"},"250":{"id":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories-3","page_id":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories#limits-and-safety","content":"Limits and safety"},"251":{"id":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories-4","page_id":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories#when-to-use-it","content":"When to use it"},"252":{"id":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories-5","page_id":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories#configuration-example","content":"Configuration example"},"253":{"id":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories-6","page_id":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories#interaction-with-differential-privacy","content":"Interaction with differential privacy"},"254":{"id":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories-7","page_id":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"255":{"id":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories-8","page_id":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories#see-also","content":"See also"},"256":{"id":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories-9","page_id":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories","content":"By default, Decoy treats columns with many distinct values (>30) as free text during generation: it learns text length only, not vocabulary. For structured high-cardinality data like diagnosis codes or product SKUs, you can opt in to retain the full vocabulary and frequency distribution."},"257":{"id":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories-10","page_id":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories#the-problem-high-cardinality","content":"A healthcare or retail dataset often has columns with thousands of distinct values:"},"258":{"id":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories-11","page_id":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories#the-problem-high-cardinality","content":"ICD-10 diagnosis codes: 74,000+ codes"},"259":{"id":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories-12","page_id":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/handle-high-cardinality-categories#the-problem-high-cardinality","content":"SKU or product codes: 10,000+ identifiers"},"2