ock)"},"581":{"id":"/docs/how-to/use-parquet-10","page_id":"/docs/how-to/use-parquet","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/use-parquet#when-to-use-it","content":"Parquet required"},"582":{"id":"/docs/how-to/use-parquet-11","page_id":"/docs/how-to/use-parquet","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/use-parquet#when-to-use-it","content":"Large datasets, out-of-core runs"},"583":{"id":"/docs/how-to/use-parquet-12","page_id":"/docs/how-to/use-parquet","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/use-parquet#when-to-use-it","content":"Parquet (columnar, typed)"},"584":{"id":"/docs/how-to/use-parquet-13","page_id":"/docs/how-to/use-parquet","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/use-parquet#when-to-use-it","content":"Mixed CSV and Parquet"},"585":{"id":"/docs/how-to/use-parquet-14","page_id":"/docs/how-to/use-parquet","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/use-parquet#when-to-use-it","content":"Set `format` per source and target"},"586":{"id":"/docs/how-to/use-parquet-15","page_id":"/docs/how-to/use-parquet","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/use-parquet#when-to-use-it","content":"S3 and GCS sources and targets also take `csv` or `parquet`. Fixed-width is input\nonly."},"587":{"id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","page_id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","type":"page","content":"Work with healthcare code sets","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Guides","Handle specialized data"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets"},"588":{"id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets-0","page_id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","content":"Use ICD-10, HCPCS, NDC, and custom code set columns for masking and generation."},"589":{"id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets-1","page_id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets#what-is