e-sets-32","page_id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets#built-in-code-sets","content":"8,725"},"621":{"id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets-33","page_id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets#built-in-code-sets","content":"Outpatient procedures, durable medical equipment"},"622":{"id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets-34","page_id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets#built-in-code-sets","content":"NDC"},"623":{"id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets-35","page_id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets#built-in-code-sets","content":"Drug"},"624":{"id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets-36","page_id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets#built-in-code-sets","content":"217,019"},"625":{"id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets-37","page_id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets#built-in-code-sets","content":"Prescription and OTC medications"},"626":{"id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets-38","page_id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets#built-in-code-sets","content":"All are public domain (no license restrictions). Each corpus includes optional chapter organization for hierarchical masking (ICD-10-CM only; HCPCS and NDC are flat)."},"627":{"id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets-39","page_id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets#mask-with-a-code-set","content":"Use the `code_set` strategy to replace codes with valid alternatives:"},"628":{"id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets-40","page_id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets#code-set-masking-modes","content":"**`code_set` with no extra options** (above): Replace each code with a uniform random valid code from the corpus. All 74,719 ICD-10 codes are equally likely."},"629":{"id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets-41","page_id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets#code-set-masking-modes","content":"**`code_set` with `chapter_preserve: true`**: Keep codes in the same chapter (e.g., diagnoses starting with I for circulatory). ICD-10 chapter structure is hierarchical (I00-I99 = circulatory system); this option masks within chapter."},"630":{"id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets-42","page_id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets#code-set-masking-modes","content":"**`code_set` with `allow_real_categories: true`** (non-DP only): Sample from the observed frequency distribution of codes in your source, not uniform random. If your data has 50% hypertension (I10) and 30% diabetes (E11), the masked output preserves these proportions."},"631":{"id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets-43","page_id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets#code-set-masking-modes","content":"Combine both:"},"632":{"id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets-44","page_id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets#generate-synthetic-codes","content":"Use `type: statistical` with a code set column:"},"633":{"id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets-45","page_id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets#generate-synthetic-codes","content":"This fits a distribution snapshot of the source codes and samples from it. The generated codes match your source frequency (e.g., hypertension codes appear at the same rate as in the original data)."},"634":{"id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets-46","page_id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets#generation-options","content":"**`allow_real_categories: false`** (default under DP): Generalize rare categories to `__other__`. Use this if your source has many low-frequency codes and you want to protect them."},"635":{"id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets-47","page_id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets#generation-options","content":"**`allow_real_categories: true`** (non-DP only): Retain all observed codes, including rare ones. Generated data preserves exact frequency distribution."},"636":{"id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets-48","page_id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets#generation-options","content":"**`high_cardinality: true`**: Retain the full vocabulary of observed codes (all 1,000+ codes if present in your source). Without this, Decoy collapses codes into an `__other__` bucket if there are too many distinct values. Set this for code-set columns which naturally have high cardinality."},"637":{"id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets-49","page_id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets#upload-a-custom-code-set","content":"For codes not in the built-in sets (proprietary billing codes, internal coding schemes), upload your own:"},"638":{"id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets-50","page_id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets#custom-corpus-format","content":"Your corpus must be a Parquet file with at least these columns:"},"639":{"id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets-51","page_id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets#custom-corpus-format","content":"Required:"},"640":{"id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets-52","page_id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets#custom-corpus-format","content":"`code`: Non-null, non-empty, unique string identifier"},"641":{"id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets-53","page_id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets#custom-corpus-format","content":"`description`: String (can be empty)"},"642":{"id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets-54","page_id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets#custom-corpus-format","content":"Optional:"},"643":{"id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets-55","page_id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets#custom-corpus-format","content":"`chapter`: String or int; enables `chapter_preserve: true`"},"644":{"id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets-56","page_id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets#custom-corpus-format","content":"Store the file locally and reference it as `customer:/absolute/path/to/file.parquet`. Decoy validates the corpus at load time and fails closed if the schema is invalid."},"645":{"id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets-57","page_id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets#foreign-keys-with-code-sets","content":"Code set columns can participate in foreign key relationships. A child table can mask or generate codes from the same corpus as a parent:"},"646":{"id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets-58","page_id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets#foreign-keys-with-code-sets","content":"Referential integrity is preserved for valid codes. If a procedure row references (patient=100, diagnosis=I10), both patient\\_id and diagnosis\\_code mask independently, but the join relationship is maintained."},"647":{"id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets-59","page_id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets#pattern-preserve-frequency-and-chapter","content":"Mask diagnosis codes, keeping frequency distribution and chapter:"},"648":{"id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets-60","page_id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets#pattern-high-cardinality-generation","content":"Generate drug codes, retaining all observed codes:"},"649":{"id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets-61","page_id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets#pattern-uniform-masking-anonymization-style","content":"Mask all codes to random valid codes, no frequency preservation:"},"650":{"id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets-62","page_id":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/how-to/work-with-healthcare-code-sets#troubleshooting","content":"**Error: `code_set_