settings","content":"Binds the keys; parent, child, and this entry share it"},"941":{"id":"/docs/reference/relationships-34","page_id":"/docs/reference/relationships","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/relationships#settings","content":"`orphan_policy` values:"},"942":{"id":"/docs/reference/relationships-35","page_id":"/docs/reference/relationships","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/relationships#settings","content":"Value"},"943":{"id":"/docs/reference/relationships-36","page_id":"/docs/reference/relationships","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/relationships#settings","content":"Effect"},"944":{"id":"/docs/reference/relationships-37","page_id":"/docs/reference/relationships","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/relationships#settings","content":"`preserve`"},"945":{"id":"/docs/reference/relationships-38","page_id":"/docs/reference/relationships","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/relationships#settings","content":"Keep the orphan key as-is"},"946":{"id":"/docs/reference/relationships-39","page_id":"/docs/reference/relationships","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/relationships#settings","content":"`remap`"},"947":{"id":"/docs/reference/relationships-40","page_id":"/docs/reference/relationships","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/relationships#settings","content":"Route it through the parent strategy for a fresh value"},"948":{"id":"/docs/reference/relationships-41","page_id":"/docs/reference/relationships","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/relationships#settings","content":"`warn`"},"949":{"id":"/docs/reference/relationships-42","page_id":"/docs/reference/relationships","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/relationships#settings","content":"Keep it, emit one aggregated warning"},"950":{"id":"/docs/reference/relationships-43","page_id":"/docs/reference/relationships","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/relationships#settings","content":"`fail`"},"951":{"id":"/docs/reference/relationships-44","page_id":"/docs/reference/relationships","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/relationships#settings","content":"Abort with `orphan_fk_violation`"},"952":{"id":"/docs/reference/relationships-45","page_id":"/docs/reference/relationships","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/relationships#shapes","content":"All shapes are deterministic and byte-stable across runs given the same seed. A\nnull key passes through as null, not an orphan."},"953":{"id":"/docs/reference/relationships-46","page_id":"/docs/reference/relationships","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/relationships#one-to-many-and-one-to-one","content":"One parent, one child table. Same config whether each parent has one match or\nmany."},"954":{"id":"/docs/reference/relationships-47","page_id":"/docs/reference/relationships","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/relationships#composite-key","content":"Multi-column key. Both sides list the columns in the same order."},"955":{"id":"/docs/reference/relationships-48","page_id":"/docs/reference/relationships","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/relationships#self-referential","content":"Parent and child are the same table (an employee's manager is an employee)."},"956":{"id":"/docs/reference/relationships-49","page_id":"/docs/reference/relationships","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/relationships#multiple-children","content":"One parent key referenced by several tables. Add a child entry per table."},"957":{"id":"/docs/reference/relationships-50","page_id":"/docs/reference/relationships","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/relationships#chain-multi-hop","content":"A to B to C. One entry per edge."},"958":{"id":"/docs/reference/relationships-51","page_id":"/docs/reference/relationships","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/relationships#chain-multi-hop","content":"For a full runnable config with sources, tables, and targets, see\nMask a folder with foreign keys."},"959":{"id":"/docs/start/demo","page_id":"/docs/start/demo","type":"page","content":"Demo","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Get started"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/start/demo"},"960":{"id":"/docs/start/demo-0","page_id":"/docs/start/demo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/start/demo","content":"Run the bundled decoy demo to see a scan-then-mask walkthrough on sample data, no config or input file required."},"961":{"id":"/docs/start/demo-1","page_id":"/docs/start/demo","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/start/demo#run-it","content":"Run it"},"962":{"id":"/docs/start/demo-2","page_id":"/docs/start/demo","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/start/demo#what-each-step-does","content":"What each step does"},"963":{"id":"/docs/start/demo-3","page_id":"/docs/start/demo","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/start/demo#inspect-the-output","content":"Inspect the output"},"964":{"id":"/docs/start/demo-4","page_id":"/docs/start/demo","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/start/demo#next","content":"Next"},"965":{"id":"/docs/start/demo-5","page_id":"/docs/start/demo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/start/demo","content":"`decoy demo` runs a full scan-then-mask walkthrough on a bundled sample\ndataset. It needs no input file and no pipeline config, which makes it the\nfastest way to see what Decoy does before writing anything of your own."},"966":{"id":"/docs/start/demo-6","page_id":"/docs/start/demo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/start/demo#run-it","content":"Everything lands in `./decoy_demo/` by default (override with `--dir`).\n`decoy demo --json` runs the same three steps but prints a structured\nsummary instead of the cards above:"},"967":{"id":"/docs/start/demo-7","page_id":"/docs/start/demo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/start/demo#what-each-step-does","content":"**\\[1/3] Writing sample dataset.** Decoy writes a 10-row synthetic customer\ntable to `decoy_demo/customers.csv`, with columns you'd expect to find in a\nreal customer export:"},"968":{"id":"/docs/start/demo-8","page_id":"/docs/start/demo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/start/demo#what-each-step-does","content":"**\\[2/3] Scanning with STORM.** STORM profiles the file column by column and\nwrites its findings to `decoy_demo/scan.json`: inferred type, distinct\ncount, format pattern, and any PII detector matches, per column. This is\nthe same profiling step `decoy storm analyze` runs on your own files, and\nthe same step `decoy init your_file.csv` runs before scaffolding a\ncolumn-aware pipeline. On your own data, STORM's findings are suggestions\nyou review before anything runs, never an automatic classification; see\nSTORM. The demo skips that review step so the\nwalkthrough completes in one command, using a pipeline Decoy scaffolds for\nyou (`decoy_demo/pipeline.yaml`) from the scan."},"969":{"id":"/docs/start/demo-9","page_id":"/docs/start/demo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/start/demo#what-each-step-does","content":"**\\[3/3] Running V2 masking pipeline.** Decoy runs the scaffolded pipeline\nagainst `customers.csv` and writes `customers_masked.csv`. The summary\npanel reports the scaffolded pipeline's verdict: of the 8 source columns, 6\nwere treated as PII and masked (`first_name`, `last_name`, `email`, `ssn`,\n`dob`, `zip`); `customer_id` was redacted separately as a direct row\nidentifier, and `gender` passed through unchanged."},"970":{"id":"/docs/start/demo-10","page_id":"/docs/start/demo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/start/demo#inspect-the-output","content":"Names and emails were swapped for synthetic values from the `faker`\nstrategy; `customer_id`, `ssn`, `dob`, and `zip` were redacted to a\nconstant; `gender` passed through. `decoy_demo/pipeline.yaml` is a regular\npipeline config, readable and editable the same as anything `decoy init`\nproduces, so it is a second, worked example alongside the one in\nQuickstart."},"971":{"id":"/docs/start/demo-11","page_id":"/docs/start/demo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/start/demo#next","content":"Quickstart runs the same shape of pipeline\nagainst your own file, with the config-validate-run flow spelled out."},"972":{"id":"/docs/start/demo-12","page_id":"/docs/start/demo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/start/demo#next","content":"Scan for PII covers `storm analyze` on your\nown data and reviewing its findings before you build a pipeline from\nthem."},"973":{"id":"/docs/start/demo-13","page_id":"/docs/start/demo","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/start/demo#next","content":"STORM explains why STORM's output is always a\nsuggestion you confirm, never an automatic classification."},"974":{"id":"/docs/start/install","page_id":"/docs/start/install","type":"page","content":"Install","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Get started"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/start/install"},"975":{"id":"/docs/start/install-0","page_id":"/docs/start/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/start/install","content":"Install the decoy CLI, check your environment with decoy doctor, and understand the license."},"976":{"id":"/docs/start/install-1","page_id":"/docs/start/install","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/start/install#requirements","content":"Requirements"},"977":{"id":"/docs/start/install-2","page_id":"/docs/start/install","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/start/install#install-from-source","content":"Install from source"},"978":{"id":"/docs/start/install-3","page_id":"/docs/start/install","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/start/install#check-the-install","content":"Check the install"},"979":{"id":"/docs/start/install-4","page_id":"/docs/start/install","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/start/install#license","content":"License"},"980":{"id":"/docs/start/install-5","page_id":"/docs/start/install","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/start/install#next","content":"Next"},"981":{"id":"/docs/start/install-6","page_id":"/docs/start/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/start/install#requirements","content":"Python 3.10, 3.11, or 3.12."},"982":{"id":"/docs/start/install-7","page_id":"/docs/start/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/start/install#requirements","content":"Git and a source checkout of `decoy`\nand `decoy-engine`. `decoy`\n(the CLI) depends on `decoy-engine` (the data-plane library); both install\ntogether."},"983":{"id":"/docs/start/install-8","page_id":"/docs/start/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/start/install#requirements","content":"`pip install decoy-cli` is the install command you will use once Decoy\nreaches general availability (the console script stays `decoy`; the\nPyPI distribution is named `decoy-cli`). Today, install from source as\ndescribed below."},"984":{"id":"/docs/start/install-9","page_id":"/docs/start/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/start/install#install-from-source","content":"This is the install path that works right now: clone both repos and install\neach in editable mode into a virtual environment."},"985":{"id":"/docs/start/install-10","page_id":"/docs/start/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/start/install#install-from-source","content":"The console script is `decoy`, even though the PyPI distribution name will\nbe `decoy-cli` at general availability (the import package and CLI stay\nshort; `decoy-cli` on the index just says plainly what the package is)."},"986":{"id":"/docs/start/install-11","page_id":"/docs/start/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/start/install#check-the-install","content":"Verify the CLI can see its runtime dependencies with `decoy doctor`:"},"987":{"id":"/docs/start/install-12","page_id":"/docs/start/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/start/install#check-the-install","content":"`doctor` exits `0` when every hard requirement is present. A missing hard\nrequirement (`decoy_engine` itself) is a non-zero exit; missing soft\nrequirements print a warning but do not fail the check, since each one gates\na specific feature (Arrow/Parquet support, the Polars execution adapter,\nderived-column expressions, checksum-based ID validation) rather than the\nCLI as a whole. `decoy doctor --json` emits the same report as JSON for CI\nor support tooling; `decoy doctor --quiet` runs silently and reports health\nonly through its exit code."},"988":{"id":"/docs/start/install-13","page_id":"/docs/start/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/start/install#check-the-install","content":"Confirm the version directly with:"},"989":{"id":"/docs/start/install-14","page_id":"/docs/start/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/start/install#license","content":"`decoy` is source-available under the Business Source License 1.1\n(BUSL-1.1). The source is readable, and non-commercial and\ninternal-business use is permitted under the license's Additional Use\nGrant; running a competing commercial service on top of it is restricted.\nFull terms, including the change-date conversion clause, are in the\n`LICENSE.md` file in your checkout."},"990":{"id":"/docs/start/install-15","page_id":"/docs/start/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/start/install#license","content":"The CLI runs entirely locally: there is no server, no account, and no\ntelemetry phone-home. Input and output data stay on your machine unless a\npipeline's own `targets:` say otherwise."},"991":{"id":"/docs/start/install-16","page_id":"/docs/start/install","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/start/install#next","content":"Continue to Quickstart to run your first masked\nfile, or jump to Demo for a zero-setup walkthrough on\nbundled sample data."},"992":{"id":"/docs/start/quickstart","page_id":"/docs/start/quickstart","type":"page","content":"Quickstart","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Get started"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/start/quickstart"},"993":{"id":"/docs/start/quickstart-0","page_id":"/docs/start/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/start/quickstart","content":"From a CSV to a masked CSV with the decoy CLI, using a scaffolded pipeline, config validation, and a run."},"994":{"id":"/docs/start/quickstart-1","page_id":"/docs/start/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/start/quickstart#1-a-csv-to-mask","content":"1\\. A CSV to mask"},"995":{"id":"/docs/start/quickstart-2","page_id":"/docs/start/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/start/quickstart#2-scaffold-a-pipeline","content":"2\\. Scaffold a pipeline"},"996":{"id":"/docs/start/quickstart-3","page_id":"/docs/start/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/start/quickstart#3-validate-the-config","content":"3\\. Validate the config"},"997":{"id":"/docs/start/quickstart-4","page_id":"/docs/start/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/start/quickstart#4-run-the-pipeline","content":"4\\. Run the pipeline"},"998":{"id":"/docs/start/quickstart-5","page_id":"/docs/start/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/start/quickstart#5-inspect-the-output","content":"5\\. Inspect the output"},"999":{"id":"/docs/start/quickstart-6","page_id":"/docs/start/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/start/quickstart#next","content":"Next"},"1000":{"id":"/docs/start/quickstart-7","page_id":"/docs/start/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/start/quickstart","content":"This walks through the shortest real path: a CSV with sensitive columns in,\na masked CSV out, using a scaffolded pipeline instead of hand-writing YAML\nfrom scratch. It assumes `decoy` is installed; see Install\nif it is not."},"1001":{"id":"/docs/start/quickstart-8","page_id":"/docs/start/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/start/quickstart#1-a-csv-to-mask","content":"Start with a small file, `input.csv`:"},"1002":{"id":"/docs/start/quickstart-9","page_id":"/docs/start/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/start/quickstart#2-scaffold-a-pipeline","content":"`decoy init` writes a starter `pipeline.yaml` for you. It normally runs as a\nshort interactive Q\\&A; the fastest path for a first look is a bundled\npreset:"},"1003":{"id":"/docs/start/quickstart-10","page_id":"/docs/start/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/start/quickstart#2-scaffold-a-pipeline","content":"The `minimal` preset scaffolds the smallest sensible pipeline: name and email\nswapped for synthetic values, SSN redacted, everything else passed through.\nIt already points at `./input.csv` and `./output.csv`, which matches the file\nabove, so nothing needs editing for this walkthrough:"},"1004":{"id":"/docs/start/quickstart-11","page_id":"/docs/start/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/start/quickstart#2-scaffold-a-pipeline","content":"On your own data, point `sources.people.path` at your file and edit the\n`columns:` list to match: pick a strategy per column\nyou want to change, and leave the rest as `passthrough`. If you scaffold with\n`decoy init your_file.csv` instead of a preset, STORM profiles the file first\nand writes a column-aware pipeline with a `# REVIEW:` comment above every\nstrategy it inferred, so you can read and confirm each one before running it,\nthe same \"suggestions, not classification\" review step described in\nSTORM."},"1005":{"id":"/docs/start/quickstart-12","page_id":"/docs/start/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/start/quickstart#3-validate-the-config","content":"Check the YAML against the engine's pipeline schema before touching any\ndata:"},"1006":{"id":"/docs/start/quickstart-13","page_id":"/docs/start/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/start/quickstart#3-validate-the-config","content":"`validate config` exits `0` on a well-formed config and non-zero on a parse\nor schema error (an unknown provider, a bad strategy name, malformed YAML),\nso it is a fast pre-flight check to run in CI before `decoy run`. It checks\nconfig well-formedness, not every runtime constraint: a strategy that needs\na `namespace` (like `hash`) but doesn't have one still passes `validate\nconfig` and is only caught when you `decoy run` it."},"1007":{"id":"/docs/start/quickstart-14","page_id":"/docs/start/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/start/quickstart#5-inspect-the-output","content":"Names and emails were replaced with synthetic values from the `faker`\nstrategy's providers, `ssn` was redacted to a constant, and\n`account_status` passed through unchanged. Because `global_settings.seed`\nis fixed, the same config against the same input always produces this same\noutput, run after run."},"1008":{"id":"/docs/start/quickstart-15","page_id":"/docs/start/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/start/quickstart#5-inspect-the-output","content":"A fixed `seed` is deterministic on one box across runs. For output that\nis also stable across different machines, mask with a shared secret\ninstead: see Keys and vault."},"1009":{"id":"/docs/start/quickstart-16","page_id":"/docs/start/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/start/quickstart#next","content":"Try Demo for a zero-setup walkthrough on bundled\nsample data, including a STORM scan step."},"1010":{"id":"/docs/start/quickstart-17","page_id":"/docs/start/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/start/quickstart#next","content":"See the how-to guides for masking recipes that\nbuild on this one: foreign-key-aware folders, synthetic generation, and\nCI usage."},"1011":{"id":"/docs/start/quickstart-18","page_id":"/docs/start/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/start/quickstart#next","content":"Browse Strategies for the full list of mask\nstrategies this pipeline could use."},"1012":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/catalog","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/catalog","type":"page","content":"decoy catalog","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","CLI reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/cli/catalog"},"1013":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/catalog-0","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/catalog","content":"LOCAL metadata catalog for data