ntent":"Per column: null-count delta, unique-count delta"},"1695":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/report-120","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/report","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/report#decoy-report-diff","content":"What diff does NOT compare:"},"1696":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/report-121","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/report","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/report#decoy-report-diff","content":"Raw row or cell values (never -- evidence-safe by design)"},"1697":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/report-122","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/report","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/report#decoy-report-diff","content":"Platform-managed state, audit logs, or remote job history"},"1698":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/report-123","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/report","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/report#decoy-report-diff","content":"Pipeline config changes (use `decoy report compare` for manifest-level diff)"},"1699":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/report-124","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/report","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/report#decoy-report-diff","content":"Scope and limitations:"},"1700":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/report-125","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/report","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/report#decoy-report-diff","content":"Requires both runs to have evidence files (`decoy run --evidence-out`)."},"1701":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/report-126","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/report","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/report#decoy-report-diff","content":"Requires the output files referenced in the evidence manifests to still\nexist at their recorded paths."},"1702":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/report-127","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/report","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/report#decoy-report-diff","content":"Compares aggregate counts only -- not a full row-by-row diff."},"1703":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/report-128","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/report","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/report#decoy-report-diff","content":"Methodology: pandas.Series.nunique() / .isnull().sum() for column-level\ncounts (pandas v2.x). No novel statistical method is used."},"1704":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/report-129","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/report","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/report#decoy-report-diff","content":"See also: decoy report compare (manifest-level), decoy jobs list."},"1705":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/run","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/run","type":"page","content":"decoy run","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","CLI reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/cli/run"},"1706":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/run-0","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/run","content":"Run a decoy pipeline from a YAML config."},"1707":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/run-1","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/run","content":"Run a decoy pipeline from a YAML config."},"1708":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/run-2","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/run","content":"Use this to execute a masking or synthetic-generation job described in\nYAML. The engine handles its own logging per the YAML's `logging:`\nsection; flags here only affect CLI-side output."},"1709":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/run-3","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/run","content":"**Usage**:"},"1710":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/run-4","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/run","content":"**Arguments**:"},"1711":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/run-5","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/run","content":"`CONFIG`: Path to the YAML pipeline config.  \\[required]"},"1712":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/run-6","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/run","content":"**Options**:"},"1713":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/run-7","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/run","content":"`-m, --mode [mask|generate]`: Operation: mask existing data or generate synthetic data.  \\[default: mask]"},"1714":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/run-8","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/run","content":"`--json`: Emit a structured JSON result on stdout. Progress goes to stderr."},"1715":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/run-9","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/run","content":"`-q, --quiet`: Suppress stdout. Errors still go to stderr; exit code carries success."},"1716":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/run-10","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/run","content":"`-v, --verbose`: Enable debug-level CLI logs on stderr."},"1717":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/run-11","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/run","content":"`--master-key TEXT`: 64-char hex master key for keyed deterministic SYNTHETIC GENERATION only (generate\\_columns:). Same key + same --key-label always yield bitwise-identical generated output across runs and machines. Reads DECOY\\_MASTER\\_KEY env var when omitted; without either, generation falls back to the legacy seeded path (per-input deterministic but not portable). This flag does NOT affect masking -- masking's keyed determinism is configured separately via '--mask-secret' (or the pipeline YAML's 'global\\_settings.mask\\_secret\\_ref'), never this flag or its env var. See: decoy explain keys.  \\[env var: DECOY\\_MASTER\\_KEY]"},"1718":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/run-12","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/run","content":"`--mask-secret TEXT`: env:NAME or file:/PATH pointing at a >=32-byte mask secret for keyed masking (mask: strategies -- fpe, hash, date\\_shift, and others). Independent of --master-key (which is generation-only). Sets 'global\\_settings.mask\\_secret\\_ref' for this run; an error if the YAML already sets it. Explicit flag only -- it deliberately has NO env var, because the ref it carries (e.g. 'env:DECOY\\_MASK\\_SECRET') already indirects through the environment; a second env layer would absorb the raw exported secret as this flag's value. See: decoy explain keys."},"1719":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/run-13","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/run","content":"`--chunked`: Stream the source through the engine chunk-by-chunk, for inputs too large to load whole. Works for mask configs whose every strategy is value-keyed (hash, fpe, redact, truncate, text\\_redact, date\\_shift, bucketize), plus faker/categorical when deterministic with an explicit pool\\_size / categories declared in config; output is byte-identical to a plain run. Sources/targets may be CSV or Parquet. See: decoy explain chunked."},"1720":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/run-14","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/run","content":"`--chunk-size INTEGER RANGE`: Rows per chunk in --chunked mode.  \\[default: 100000; x>=1]"},"1721":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/run-15","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/run","content":"`--vault PATH`: Write the token vault (encrypted source-to-masked map for vault: true columns) to this path. The vault plus the config re-identify every vaulted value: store them separately and never alongside the masked output. Needs the engine's vault extra (cryptography)."},"1722":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/run-16","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/run","content":"`--substrate TEXT`: Execution substrate for --chunked runs: pandas (default) or polars. Non-chunked (plain) runs always use the engine's pandas adapter (the V2 unified run\\_pipeline path); this flag and the DECOY\\_SUBSTRATE env var are only consulted for --chunked runs. Setting either on a plain run emits a warning to stderr and is otherwise ignored. Cross-substrate outputs are value-equal; CSV bytes may differ only via Arrow type-width drift, which CSV does not carry.  \\[env var: DECOY\\_SUBSTRATE]"},"1723":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/run-17","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/run","content":"`--key-label TEXT`: Stable namespace string for the --master-key generation key hierarchy (synthetic generation only, not masking). Required when --master-key is set. Pick something durable (e.g. 'customers\\_q4'); changing it produces different generated output. CLI flag only -- PipelineConfig forbids unknown top-level keys, so there is no YAML equivalent."},"1724":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/run-18","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/run","content":"`--evidence-out PATH`: Write a local evidence manifest (JSON) to this path after a successful run. The manifest records pipeline hash, input/output file fingerprints, run metadata, and row counts/timings/warnings where available (these are omitted for --chunked runs). It does NOT contain raw data values. Use `decoy evidence verify` to check the manifest against current files. See: decoy explain evidence (when available)."},"1725":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/run-19","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/run","content":"`--notify TEXT`: Notify a channel after the run reaches its terminal state. Repeatable. Spec is 'kind:target': webhook:\\<url>, slack:\\<url>, email:\\<address>. Best-effort: a channel failure never changes the run's exit code. Webhook signing key from DECOY\\_NOTIFY\\_WEBHOOK\\_SECRET (unsigned if unset); SMTP from DECOY\\_NOTIFY\\_SMTP\\_HOST/\\_PORT/\\_USER/\\_PASS/\\_FROM. Nothing is persisted to .decoy/workspace.json -- targets and secrets are flags/env only, never written to disk."},"1726":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/run-20","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/run","content":"`--notify-on [success|failure|always]`: Which terminal outcome(s) to notify on: success, failure, or always.  \\[default: always]"},"1727":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/run-21","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/run","content":"`--help`: Show this message and exit."},"1728":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/run-22","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/run","content":"Examples:"},"1729":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/run-23","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/run","content":"decoy run pipeline.yaml\nRun with default mode (mask)."},"1730":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/run-24","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/run","content":"decoy run pipeline.yaml --json\nSuppress chrome and emit a structured result for scripting."},"1731":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/run-25","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/run","content":"decoy run pipeline.yaml --chunked --chunk-size 100000\nStream a large source through the engine instead of loading it whole.\n(See: decoy explain chunked.)"},"1732":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/run-26","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/run","content":"decoy run pipeline.yaml --vault vault.bin\nWrite an encrypted token vault for columns marked `vault: true`, so\nthey can be recovered later with `decoy unmask`. (See: decoy explain vault.)"},"1733":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/run-27","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/run","content":"decoy run pipeline.yaml --chunked --substrate polars\nStream with polars instead of the chunked-path pandas default.\n(--substrate only affects --chunked runs; plain runs always use pandas.\nSee: decoy explain substrate.)"},"1734":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/run-28","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/run","content":"decoy run pipeline.yaml --notify webhook:https\\://hooks.example.com/x\nNotify a webhook after the run reaches its terminal state. Repeatable;\nkind in webhook/slack/email. Best-effort: a channel failure never\nchanges the run's exit code. Webhook signing key from\nDECOY\\_NOTIFY\\_WEBHOOK\\_SECRET; SMTP from DECOY\\_NOTIFY\\_SMTP\\_HOST/\\_PORT/\n\\_USER/\\_PASS/\\_FROM. Nothing is persisted to .decoy/workspace.json."},"1735":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/run-29","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/run","content":"decoy run pipeline.yaml --notify slack:https\\://hooks.slack.com/services/x --notify-on failure\nOnly notify on a failed run."},"1736":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/run-30","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/run","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/run","content":"See also: decoy validate config, decoy validate distribution, decoy explain chunked, decoy explain vault."},"1737":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/schema","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/schema","type":"page","content":"decoy schema","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","CLI reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/cli/schema"},"1738":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/schema-0","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/schema","content":"Print the PipelineConfig JSON Schema to stdout."},"1739":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/schema-1","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/schema","content":"Print the PipelineConfig JSON Schema to stdout."},"1740":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/schema-2","page_id":"/docs/refer