cs/reference/cli/validate-13","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","content":"`distribution`: Recompute distribution fidelity between a..."},"2039":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate-14","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/validate#decoy-validate-config","content":"Validate a decoy pipeline config without running it."},"2040":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate-15","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/validate#decoy-validate-config","content":"Use this in CI or before a long run to fail fast on a bad YAML. Exits 0\non a well-formed config, 1 on a parse / schema error or a config-level\nplan-compile error (unknown provider, non-poolable provider on the\nfaker/pool path, missing deterministic namespace)."},"2041":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate-16","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/validate#decoy-validate-config","content":"With --fail-on-warning, also exits non-zero when advisory warnings fire\n(e.g. an output file already exists and would be overwritten on run)."},"2042":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate-17","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/validate#decoy-validate-config","content":"**Usage**:"},"2043":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate-18","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/validate#decoy-validate-config","content":"**Arguments**:"},"2044":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate-19","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/validate#decoy-validate-config","content":"`CONFIG`: Path to the YAML pipeline config to validate.  \\[required]"},"2045":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate-20","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/validate#decoy-validate-config","content":"**Options**:"},"2046":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate-21","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/validate#decoy-validate-config","content":"`--json`: Emit a structured JSON result on stdout. Errors still go to stderr."},"2047":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate-22","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/validate#decoy-validate-config","content":"`-q, --quiet`: Suppress stdout. Errors still go to stderr; exit code carries the result."},"2048":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate-23","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/validate#decoy-validate-config","content":"`-v, --verbose`: Enable debug-level CLI logs on stderr."},"2049":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate-24","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/validate#decoy-validate-config","content":"`--fail-on-warning`: Exit non-zero if any advisory warning fires (e.g. output target exists). Enables CI gates that treat warnings as blocking."},"2050":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate-25","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/validate#decoy-validate-config","content":"`--help`: Show this message and exit."},"2051":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate-26","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/validate#decoy-validate-config","content":"Examples:"},"2052":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate-27","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/validate#decoy-validate-config","content":"decoy validate config pipeline.yaml\nPrint OK on stdout when the config parses."},"2053":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate-28","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/validate#decoy-validate-config","content":"decoy validate config pipeline.yaml --json\nEmit a structured JSON result (multi-message) for scripting."},"2054":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate-29","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/validate#decoy-validate-config","content":"decoy validate config pipeline.yaml --quiet\nStay silent on success; exit code carries the result."},"2055":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate-30","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/validate#decoy-validate-config","content":"decoy validate config pipeline.yaml --fail-on-warning\nExit non-zero if any advisory warning fires (e.g. output target exists)."},"2056":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate-31","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/validate#decoy-validate-config","content":"See also: decoy run, decoy validate distribution."},"2057":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate-32","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/validate#decoy-validate-distribution","content":"Recompute distribution fidelity between a source and an output CSV."},"2058":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate-33","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/validate#decoy-validate-distribution","content":"The engine owns every metric and the letter grade; this command\ncomputes no fidelity number itself. Reads both CSVs fresh on every\ninvocation (pure, repeatable) -- the CLI's local evidence manifest\nrecords file fingerprints but not the raw frames, so recomputing from\nthe two files is the only honest source for this number."},"2059":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate-34","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/validate#decoy-validate-distribution","content":"Exit codes: 0 when the policy verdict is 'pass' (or 'warn' without\n\\--fail-on-warning); EXIT\\_FINDINGS (4) when the verdict is 'fail', or\n'warn' with --fail-on-warning set. This mirrors `decoy storm\nintegrity`'s exit-code contract -- a data-audit verb that reports\nfindings, not a run that crashed -- rather than EXIT\\_RUNTIME (reserved\nfor the CLI/engine blowing up unexpectedly)."},"2060":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate-35","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/validate#decoy-validate-distribution","content":"**Usage**:"},"2061":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate-36","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/validate#decoy-validate-distribution","content":"**Arguments**:"},"2062":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate-37","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/validate#decoy-validate-distribution","content":"`SOURCE`: Pre-mask / pre-generate source CSV (ground truth).  \\[required]"},"2063":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate-38","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/validate#decoy-validate-distribution","content":"`OUTPUT`: Post-mask / post-generate output CSV to check.  \\[required]"},"2064":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate-39","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/validate#decoy-validate-distribution","content":"**Options**:"},"2065":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate-40","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/validate#decoy-validate-distribution","content":"`--joint TEXT`: Column pair 'a,b' to also score jointly (repeatable)."},"2066":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate-41","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/validate#decoy-validate-distribution","content":"`--generate`: Output is synthetic generation, not masking: row counts may legitimately differ (sets expect\\_row\\_parity=False). Default assumes masking (row parity expected)."},"2067":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate-42","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/validate#decoy-validate-distribution","content":"`--config FILE`: Pipeline YAML naming each column's strategy, so intentional loss (hash, bucketize, faker, ...) is not flagged as accidental drift. Without it, per-column policy checks run on defaults only."},"2068":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate-43","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/validate#decoy-validate-distribution","content":"`--policy FILE`: A quality-policy config (YAML or JSON: mode / thresholds / strategy\\_expectations) overriding --mode / --min-grade / --min-score."},"2069":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate-44","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/validate#decoy-validate-distribution","content":"`--mode TEXT`: report (record only, verdict always pass) | warn (violations promote verdict to warn) | fail (violations promote verdict to fail). Ignored when --policy sets its own mode.  \\[default: report]"},"2070":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate-45","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/validate#decoy-validate-distribution","content":"`--min-grade TEXT`: Shorthand: minimum letter grade (A/B/C/D) the overall score must reach."},"2071":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate-46","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/validate#decoy-validate-distribution","content":"`--min-score FLOAT`: Shorthand: minimum overall\\_score in \\[0, 1]."},"2072":{"id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate-47","page_id":"/docs/reference/cli/validate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/cli/validate#decoy-validate-distribution","content":"`--fail-on-warning`: Also exit non-zero (EXIT\\_FINDING