iguration/schema-58","page_id":"/docs/reference/configuration/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/configuration/schema#key-nested-objects","content":"**`GenerateColumnConfig`** (`tables[].generate_columns[]`): one synthesis\ncolumn. Required: `name`, `type` (one of `faker`, `sequence`,\n`categorical`, `formula`, `reference`, `statistical`, `derived`,\n`derived_aggregate`, `grouped_series`, `windowed_date`, `group_key`).\nPer-type parameters ride flat on the same object (`extra: allow`), not\nnested under a `config:` key."},"2277":{"id":"/docs/reference/configuration/schema-59","page_id":"/docs/reference/configuration/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/configuration/schema#key-nested-objects","content":"**`RelationshipConfig`** (`relationships[]`): one FK edge. `parent` and\neach entry in `children` are a `RelationshipEnd` (`table` + `columns`,\n`columns` supports composite keys). `orphan_policy` is required: one of\n`preserve`, `remap`, `warn`, `fail`."},"2278":{"id":"/docs/reference/configuration/schema-60","page_id":"/docs/reference/configuration/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/configuration/schema#key-nested-objects","content":"**`TableConfig`** (`tables[]`): a table is either a mask table (`columns`,\nfed by a `sources` entry) or a generate table (`generate_columns` +\n`row_count`, no source), not both. `transforms` is an ordered list of\nshaping ops (`filter`, `sort`, `limit`, `dedupe`, `derive`, `drop_column`),\neach discriminated on its own `op` field."},"2279":{"id":"/docs/reference/configuration/schema-61","page_id":"/docs/reference/configuration/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/configuration/schema#key-nested-objects","content":"**`GlobalSettings`**: `seed` is the only required field. `mask_secret_ref`\nis a reference (`env:NAME` or `file:/path`), never the secret itself, see\nkeys and the vault."},"2280":{"id":"/docs/reference/configuration/schema-62","page_id":"/docs/reference/configuration/schema","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/configuration/schema#next","content":"See strategy before/after for what a\n`strategy` value actually does to data, and connectors\nfor the `sources:` / `targets:` backends."},"2281":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/bucket-perturb","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/bucket-perturb","type":"page","content":"bucket_perturb","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Strategies","Dates and geography"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/strategies/bucket-perturb"},"2282":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/bucket-perturb-0","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/bucket-perturb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/bucket-perturb","content":"Snap a date to a deterministic position in its week, month, or quarter."},"2283":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/bucket-perturb-1","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/bucket-perturb","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/strategies/bucket-perturb#settings","content":"Settings"},"2284":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/bucket-perturb-2","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/bucket-perturb","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/strategies/bucket-perturb#example","content":"Example"},"2285":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/bucket-perturb-3","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/bucket-perturb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/bucket-perturb","content":"Moves a date to a deterministic position inside its ISO week, calendar month, or\ncalendar quarter, so the date shifts within a bounded period and the same input\nalways lands the same way. This is a date strategy; it does not apply to numbers."},"2286":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/bucket-perturb-4","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/bucket-perturb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/bucket-perturb#settings","content":"Option"},"2287":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/bucket-perturb-5","page_id":"/docs/referenc