e#settings","content":"`keep`"},"2808":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate-13","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate#settings","content":"string"},"2809":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate-14","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate#settings","content":"`head`"},"2810":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate-15","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate#settings","content":"`head` keeps the first N, `tail` keeps the last N"},"2811":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate-16","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate#settings","content":"For the full parameter set, run `decoy strategies inspect truncate`."},"2812":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate-17","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate#example","content":"Before"},"2813":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate-18","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate#example","content":"After"},"2814":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate-19","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate#example","content":"`94107`"},"2815":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate-20","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate#example","content":"`941`"},"2816":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate-21","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate#example","content":"`73301`"},"2817":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate-22","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate#example","content":"`733`"},"2818":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate-23","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate#example","content":"`10001`"},"2819":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate-24","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/truncate#example","content":"`100`"},"2820":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date","type":"page","content":"windowed_date","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Strategies","Dates and geography"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date"},"2821":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date-0","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date","content":"Move a date to a random point in a window."},"2822":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date-1","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date#settings","content":"Settings"},"2823":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date-2","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date#example","content":"Example"},"2824":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date-3","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date","content":"Shifts each date to a random offset within a window relative to an anchor. Unlike\n`date_shift`, the output lands in a bounded window rather than keeping a fixed\nper-value offset. `distribution` biases where in the window the date falls."},"2825":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date-4","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date#settings","content":"Option"},"2826":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date-5","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date#settings","content":"Type"},"2827":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date-6","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date#settings","content":"Default"},"2828":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date-7","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date#settings","content":"Description"},"2829":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date-8","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date#settings","content":"`anchor`"},"2830":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date-9","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date#settings","content":"string"},"2831":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date-10","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date#settings","content":"required"},"2832":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date-11","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date#settings","content":"The reference date the window is measured from"},"2833":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date-12","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date#settings","content":"`min_days`"},"2834":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date-13","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date#settings","content":"integer"},"2835":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date-14","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date#settings","content":"`0`"},"2836":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date-15","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date#settings","content":"Earliest offset from the anchor"},"2837":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date-16","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date#settings","content":"`max_days`"},"2838":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date-17","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date#settings","content":"integer"},"2839":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date-18","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date#settings","content":"required"},"2840":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date-19","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date#settings","content":"Latest offset from the anchor"},"2841":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date-20","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date#settings","content":"`distribution`"},"2842":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date-21","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date#settings","content":"string"},"2843":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date-22","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date#settings","content":"`uniform`"},"2844":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date-23","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date#settings","content":"`uniform`, `early`, or `late` bias within the window"},"2845":{"id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date-24","page_id":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/strategies/windowed-date#settings","content":"For the full parameter set, run `decoy strategies inspect windowed_date`."},"2846":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs","type":"page","content":"GCS","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Connectors"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs"},"2847":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs-0","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs","content":"Pipeline YAML shape and credentials for a Google Cloud Storage source or target."},"2848":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs-1","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs#fields","content":"Fields"},"2849":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs-2","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs#credentials","content":"Credentials"},"2850":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs-3","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs#next","content":"Next"},"2851":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs-4","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs","content":"A GCS source or target names a `bucket` and an `object` (GCS calls its\nobject path `object`, not `key`, matching the GCS API). Both `csv` and\n`parquet` are supported; nothing else."},"2852":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs-5","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs","content":"This validates cleanly against the schema:"},"2853":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs-6","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs","content":"Validating a config does not mean `decoy run` will execute it end to end.\nThe standalone CLI only reads and writes `type: file` sources and\ntargets today; see connectors for the full caveat.\nThe shape below is real and is what a Decoy platform-managed run\nconsumes."},"2854":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs-7","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs#fields","content":"Field"},"2855":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs-8","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs#fields","content":"Required"},"2856":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs-9","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs#fields","content":"Notes"},"2857":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs-10","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs#fields","content":"`bucket`"},"2858":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs-11","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs#fields","content":"yes"},"2859":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs-12","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs#fields","content":"1-255 characters."},"2860":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs-13","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs#fields","content":"`object`"},"2861":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs-14","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs#fields","content":"yes"},"2862":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs-15","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs#fields","content":"The object path within the bucket."},"2863":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs-16","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs#fields","content":"`credentials_ref`"},"2864":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs-17","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs#fields","content":"no"},"2865":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs-18","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs#fields","content":"An opaque identifier a Decoy platform-managed run resolves against its own credential store. Has no effect outside the platform; the schema forbids a raw service-account key here (`additionalProperties: false`)."},"2866":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs-19","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs#fields","content":"No other fields are accepted, an unrecognized key (for example a raw\n`service_account_json`) fails `decoy validate config` rather than being\nsilently ignored."},"2867":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs-20","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs#credentials","content":"Outside the platform, GCS access is resolved by Application Default\nCredentials (ADC), not by the YAML:"},"2868":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs-21","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs#credentials","content":"`GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS` pointing at a service-account key file."},"2869":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs-22","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs#credentials","content":"`gcloud auth application-default login` user credentials."},"2870":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs-23","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs#credentials","content":"The GCE or GKE metadata service, when running on Google Cloud compute\n(including GKE workload identity)."},"2871":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs-24","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs#credentials","content":"There is no `endpoint_url` equivalent for GCS: unlike S3, the connector\ndoes not support pointing at a non-Google-hosted GCS-compatible service."},"2872":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs-25","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/gcs#next","content":"See connectors for the file-backend comparison and the\ncurrent `decoy run` execution scope, and S3 for the\nS3 equivalent."},"2873":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors","type":"page","content":"Connectors and formats","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Connectors"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/connectors"},"2874":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors-0","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors","content":"The file, S3, and GCS backends a Decoy pipeline can name as a source or target."},"2875":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors-1","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/connectors#file","content":"file"},"2876":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors-2","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/connectors#s3-and-gcs","content":"s3 and gcs"},"2877":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors-3","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/connectors#sftp","content":"sftp"},"2878":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors-4","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/connectors#credentials","content":"Credentials"},"2879":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors-5","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors","content":"A pipeline's `sources:` and `targets:` blocks each name a `type`: `file`,\n`s3`, or `gcs`. All three share the same shape everywhere else in the\nconfig, the column list, strategies, relationships, and validators do not\nchange based on where the bytes come from or go."},"2880":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors-6","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors#file","content":"Reads CSV, Parquet, or fixed-width files, and writes CSV or Parquet, on the\nlocal filesystem. This is the only backend the standalone `decoy run` command\nmoves data through today: it reads every `type: file` source into memory\nand writes every `type: file` target back out, in full, for the mask or\ngenerate run. See mask a CSV for a worked\nexample."},"2881":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors-7","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors#s3-and-gcs","content":"The pipeline schema also accepts `type: s3` and `type: gcs` source and\ntarget blocks, shown on their own pages: S3,\nGCS. Both validate with `decoy validate config` and\nboth formats are `csv` or `parquet` only, no fixed-width."},"2882":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors-8","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors#s3-and-gcs","content":"As of `decoy` 0.1.0 / `decoy-engine` 0.4.0, the standalone CLI's `run`\ncommand only materializes `type: file` sources and targets. A `type: s3`\nor `type: gcs` block in a config you run directly with `decoy run` will\nnot be read from or written to the cloud object: the CLI's local source\nloader looks for a `path` field, which S3 and GCS sources do not have.\nThese blocks are the same shape a Decoy platform-managed run consumes\n(the platform resolves credentials and streams the object on your\nbehalf); for a CLI-only workflow today, download the source to a local\nfile, mask it with `type: file`, and upload the result yourself."},"2883":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors-9","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors#sftp","content":"The engine ships an SFTP connector (`decoy_engine.connectors.sftp`, behind\nthe optional `sftp` extra) with password and private-key auth. It is not\nwired into pipeline YAML: `sources:` and `targets:` only accept `file`,\n`s3`, and `gcs` as a `type`. See SFTP for what\nexists today and what a `type: sftp` block currently does when you try it."},"2884":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors-10","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors#credentials","content":"Neither S3 nor GCS pipeline blocks carry an access key, secret key, or\nservice-account JSON field, the schema forbids unknown fields\n(`additionalProperties: false`), and those fields are not in it. Both\nbackends resolve credentials from the environment: the AWS SDK's default\ncredential chain for S3 (`AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` / `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`,\n`~/.aws/credentials`, an instance profile) and Application Default\nCredentials for GCS (`GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS`, `gcloud auth login`,\na GCE/GKE metadata service). See each connector's page for the full field\nlist."},"2885":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","type":"page","content":"S3","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Connectors"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3"},"2886":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3-0","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","content":"Pipeline YAML shape and credentials for an S3 (or S3-compatible) source or target."},"2887":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3-1","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3#fields","content":"Fields"},"2888":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3-2","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3#credentials","content":"Credentials"},"2889":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3-3","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3#next","content":"Next"},"2890":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3-4","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","content":"An S3 source or target names a `bucket` and a `key` (the S3 object path).\nBoth `csv` and `parquet` are supported; nothing else."},"2891":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3-5","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","content":"This validates cleanly against the schema:"},"2892":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3-6","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","content":"Validating a config does not mean `decoy run` will execute it end to end.\nThe standalone CLI only reads and writes `type: file` sources and\ntargets today; see connectors for the full caveat.\nThe shape below is real and is what a Decoy platform-managed run\nconsumes."},"2893":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3-7","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3#fields","content":"Field"},"2894":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3-8","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3#fields","content":"Required"},"2895":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3-9","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3#fields","content":"Notes"},"2896":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3-10","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3#fields","content":"`bucket`"},"2897":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3-11","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3#fields","content":"yes"},"2898":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3-12","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3#fields","content":"1-255 characters."},"2899":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3-13","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3#fields","content":"`key`"},"2900":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3-14","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3#fields","content":"yes"},"2901":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3-15","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3#fields","content":"The object path within the bucket."},"2902":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3-16","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3#fields","content":"`region`"},"2903":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3-17","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3#fields","content":"no"},"2904":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3-18","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3#fields","content":"Defaults to `us-east-1` on the connector; omit to use whatever the credential chain / environment implies."},"2905":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3-19","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3#fields","content":"`endpoint_url`"},"2906":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3-20","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3#fields","content":"no"},"2907":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3-21","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3#fields","content":"Override the AWS endpoint for an S3-compatible service: MinIO, Cloudflare R2, Wasabi, Backblaze B2. Leave unset for real AWS S3."},"2908":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3-22","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3#fields","content":"`credentials_ref`"},"2909":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3-23","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3#fields","content":"no"},"2910":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3-24","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3#fields","content":"An opaque identifier a Decoy platform-managed run resolves against its own credential store. Has no effect outside the platform; the schema forbids raw access keys here (`additionalProperties: false`)."},"2911":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3-25","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3#fields","content":"No other fields are accepted, an unrecognized key (for example a raw\n`access_key_id`) fails `decoy validate config` rather than being silently\nignored."},"2912":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3-26","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3#credentials","content":"Outside the platform, S3 access is resolved by the AWS SDK's default\ncredential chain, not by the YAML:"},"2913":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3-27","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3#credentials","content":"`AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` / `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` (and `AWS_SESSION_TOKEN` for\ntemporary credentials) as environment variables."},"2914":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3-28","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3#credentials","content":"`~/.aws/credentials` / `~/.aws/config`, including named profiles via\n`AWS_PROFILE`."},"2915":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3-29","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3#credentials","content":"An EC2 instance profile, ECS task role, or EKS IRSA role, when running on\nAWS compute."},"2916":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3-30","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3#credentials","content":"Point a config at an S3-compatible store (MinIO, R2, Wasabi, B2) with\n`endpoint_url`:"},"2917":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3-31","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/s3#next","content":"See connectors for the file-backend comparison and the\ncurrent `decoy run` execution scope, and GCS for\nthe Google Cloud Storage equivalent."},"2918":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/sftp","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/sftp","type":"page","content":"SFTP","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Reference","Connectors"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/connectors/sftp"},"2919":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/sftp-0","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/sftp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/sftp","content":"Current status of the SFTP connector, what exists, and what a pipeline cannot do with it yet."},"2920":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/sftp-1","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/sftp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/connectors/sftp#what-exists-at-the-connector-level","content":"What exists at the connector level"},"2921":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/sftp-2","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/sftp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/connectors/sftp#next","content":"Next"},"2922":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/sftp-3","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/sftp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/sftp","content":"`decoy-engine` ships an SFTP connector\n(`decoy_engine.connectors.sftp.SFTPFileSource` /\n`SFTPFileSink`), but it is not wired into pipeline YAML. `sources:` and\n`targets:` only accept `file`, `s3`, and `gcs` as a `type`; `sftp` is\nrejected at validation:"},"2923":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/sftp-4","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/sftp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/sftp","content":"There is no `type: sftp` source or target block to write today. This page\nexists so \"does Decoy support SFTP\" has a clear, current answer rather than\nsilence."},"2924":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/sftp-5","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/sftp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/sftp#what-exists-at-the-connector-level","content":"The connector class itself is real and unit-tested: password auth, or a\nPEM private key (RSA, Ed25519, ECDSA, DSA, auto-detected), strict host-key\nverification against `known_hosts` (no accept-any-host-key fallback), and\nstreaming reads and writes. It depends on `paramiko`, an optional extra so\ncustomers who only use S3 or GCS do not pay for it:"},"2925":{"id":"/docs/reference/connectors/sftp-6","page_id":"/docs/reference/connectors/sftp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/connectors/sftp#what-exists-at-the-connector-level","content":"That extra makes the connector importable for direct engine-SDK use; it\ndoes not add a pipeline YAML source or target type. Wiring `sftp` into\n`sources:` / `targets:` the way `s3` and `gcs` are wired is on the\nroadmap, not shipped."},"2926":