e. On your own data, STORM's findings are suggestions\nyou review before anything runs, never an automatic classification; see\nSTORM. The demo skips that review step so the\nwalkthrough completes in one command, using a pipeline Decoy scaffolds for\nyou (`decoy_demo/pipeline.yaml`) from the scan."],[969,"**\\[3/3] Running V2 masking pipeline.** Decoy runs the scaffolded pipeline\nagainst `customers.csv` and writes `customers_masked.csv`. The summary\npanel reports the scaffolded pipeline's verdict: of the 8 source columns, 6\nwere treated as PII and masked (`first_name`, `last_name`, `email`, `ssn`,\n`dob`, `zip`); `customer_id` was redacted separately as a direct row\nidentifier, and `gender` passed through unchanged."],[634,"**`allow_real_categories: false`** (default under DP): Generalize rare categories to `__other__`. Use this if your source has many low-frequency codes and you want to protect them."],[77,"**`allow_real_categories: false`** prevents the engine from releasing actual category names from your data. When set to false, high-frequency categories are generalized."],[543,"**`allow_real_categories: false`**: Prevents releasing actual category names. Set to true only if your category labels are public and non-sensitive."],[635,"**`allow_real_categories: true`** (non-DP only): Retain all observed codes, including rare ones. Generated data preserves exact frequency distribution."],[630,"**`code_set` with `allow_real_categories: true`** (non-DP only): Sample from the observed frequency distribution of codes in your source, not uniform random. If your data has 50% hypertension (I10) and 30% diabetes (E11), the masked output preserves these proportions."],[629,"**`code_set` with `chapter_preserve: true`**: Keep codes in the same chapter (e.g., diagnoses starting with I for circulatory). ICD-10 chapter structure is hierarchical (I00-I99 = circulatory system); this option masks within chapter."],[628,"**`code_set` with no extra options** (above): Replace each code with a uniform random valid code from the corpus. All 74,719 ICD-10 codes are equally likely."],[76,"**`column_schema` is required.** You declare each typed carrier (numeric, categorical, or flag column) you want DP protection for, with its type and domain (min/max for numeric, category list for categorical). Inferring the domain from the data itself leaks information at zero budget."],[542,"**`column_schema`**: List only columns you want DP coverage for. Omit columns that are not sensitive or that you want to generate without DP (e.g., dates, free text)."],[2275,"**`ColumnConfig`** (`tables[].columns[]`): one mask column. Required:\n`name`, `strategy`. Everything else, `provider`, `namespace`,\n`cardinality_mode`, `deterministic`, `scale`, `provider_config`,\n`vault`, `allow_collisions`, and more, is optional and strategy-dependent.\nSee strategy before/after for real examples."],[541,"**`delta: 1e-6`**: Failure probability. Typical choice; smaller is stronger but may degrade fidelity."],[540,"**`epsilon: 1.0`**: Moderate privacy with reasonable fidelity. Start here for most use cases."],[2276,"**`GenerateColumnConfig`** (`tables[].generate_columns[]`): one synthesis\ncolumn. Required: `name`, `type` (one of `faker`, `sequence`,\n`categorical`, `formula`, `reference`, `statistical`, `derived`,\n`derived_aggregate`, `grouped_series`, `windowed_date`, `group_key`).\nPer-type parameters ride flat on the same object (`extra: allow`), not\nnested under a `config:` key."],[2279,"**`GlobalSettings`**: `seed` is the only required field. `mask_secret_ref`\nis a reference (`env:NAME` or `file:/path`), never the secret itself, see\nkeys and the vault."],[636,"**`high_cardinality: true`**: Retain the full vocabulary of observed codes (all 1,000+ codes if present in your source). Without this, Decoy collapses codes into an `__other__` bucket if there are too many distinct values. Set this for code-set columns which naturally have high cardinality."],[379,"**`ner: true`**: Enable NER detection (requires `[ner]` extra). Detects PERSON and GPE (geopolitical entity, i.e., locations)."],[380,"**`redact_placeholder`** (optional): String to replace sensitive spans. Default is `[PII]`. Use `[REDACTED]`, `[NAME]`, `[LOCATION]`, or any custom string."],[381,"**`redact_replacement`** (alternative to placeholder): Replace with a synthetic value (e.g., a generated name) instead of a fixed placeholder. See below."],[2277,"**`RelationshipConfig`** (`relationships[]`): one FK edge. `parent` and\neach entry in `children` are a `RelationshipEnd` (`table` + `columns`,\n`columns` supports composite keys). `orphan_policy` is required: one of\n`preserve`, `remap`, `warn`, `fail`."],[2278,"**`TableConfig`** (`tables[]`): a table is either a mask table (`columns`,\nfed by a `sources` entry) or a generate table (`generate_columns` +\n`row_count`, no source), not both. `transforms` is an ordered list of\nshaping ops (`filter`, `sort`, `limit`, `dedupe`, `derive`, `drop_column`),\neach discriminated on its own `op` field."],[1049,"**Arguments**:"],[1075,"**Arguments**:"],[1114,"**Arguments**:"],[1175,"**Arguments**:"],[1196,"**Arguments**:"],[1224,"**Arguments**:"],[1241,"**Arguments**:"],[1333,"**Arguments**:"],[1382,"**Arguments**:"],[1399,"**Arguments**:"],[1418,"**Arguments**:"],[1439,"**Arguments**:"],[1468,"**Arguments**:"],[1563,"**Arguments**:"],[1595,"**Arguments**:"],[1612,"**Arguments**:"],[1626,"**Arguments**:"],[1652,"**Arguments**:"],[1679,"**Arguments**:"],[1710,"**Arguments**:"],[1777,"**Arguments**:"],[1801,"**Arguments**:"],[1819,"**Arguments**:"],[1840,"**Arguments**:"],[1857,"**Arguments**:"],[1873,"**Arguments**:"],[1926,"**Arguments**:"],[1943,"**Arguments**:"],[1988,"**Arguments**:"],[2005,"**Arguments**:"],[2043,"**Arguments**:"],[2061,"**Arguments**:"],[2120,"**Arguments**:"],[411,"**Best practice**: Run `text_redact` with NER as a first pass to catch common person names and places, then review the output manually or with a second detection pass."],[656,"**Code values change inconsistently across runs**"],[1021,"**Commands**:"],[1095,"**Commands**:"],[1167,"**Commands**:"],[1287,"**Commands**:"],[1358,"**Commands**:"],[1495,"**Commands**:"],[1547,"**Commands**:"],[1585,"**Commands**:"],[1765,"**Commands**:"],[1910,"**Commands**:"],[1971,"**Commands**:"],[2036,"**Commands**:"],[2095,"**Commands**:"],[2115,"**Commands**:"],[12,"**Concepts**: how determinism, keys, STORM,\ndisguises, and differential privacy work."],[111,"**Declare your column schema.** List every column you want DP protection for, its type, and its domain."],[72,"**Delta (δ)**: The failure probability. A small constant (typically 1e-6 or 1e-9), delta represents the chance that the guarantee is violated. In most cases, use a delta smaller than 1/n, where n is your dataset size."],[565,"**Domain must be known upfront.** You declare age domain as \\[0, 120], diagnosis codes as a fixed list. The engine does not infer these from the data."],[88,"**DP does not mean zero information leakage.** It means bounded leakage. An attacker with the synthetic data learns something, but only up to the epsilon budget."],[90,"**DP in Decoy measures by row, not person.** If a person in your source has fifty rows (claim records, lab results), removing one person removes fifty rows. The DP guarantee covers removing one row, not one person. For healthcare multi-record scenarios, this means the per-person privacy is weaker than the per-row epsilon suggests: removing a fifty-row person is a fifty-row change, far beyond the one-row guarantee. Decoy's configuration treats rows as the unit."],[89,"**DP is not anonymization.** Privacy and utility are a tradeoff. Adding noise makes the output safer to publish but less faithful to the source. You still need to review the synthetic output and decide if it is safe for your use case."],[68,"**Epsilon (ε)**: Controls privacy loss per column. Think of it as \"how much noise should we add?\" Smaller epsilon means more noise (stronger privacy), higher epsilon means less noise (better fidelity). Typical values range from 0.1 to 10."],[566,"**Epsilon is enforced.** If you exceed the declared epsilon/delta budget, the job fails with an error."],[652,"**Error: `code_set_corpus_duplicate_codes`**"],[650,"**Error: `code_set_corpus_null_code` or `code_set_corpus_empty_code`**"],[296,"**Error: `code_set_corpus_too_many_values` or similar**"],[419,"**Error: `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'spacy'`**"],[421,"**Error: `OSError: [E050] Can't find model 'en_core_web_sm'`**"],[607,"**Generate**: sample synthetic codes from a distribution fitted off your source"],[10,"**Get started**: install the CLI and mask your first\nfile."],[11,"**Guides**: task recipes for masking, synthetic\ngeneration, foreign keys, subsetting, Parquet, and CI."],[554,"**Increase delta** (higher failure probability, better fidelity): try 1e-5 (but accept higher risk)"],[553,"**Increase epsilon** (weaker privacy, better fidelity): try 2.0 or 3.0"],[372,"**Input**: \"Patient John Smith from Boston was admitted to Mass General\""],[128,"**It is not a compliance certification.** A Disguise named `hipaa` encodes\none engineering-team's reasonable reading of a common identifier set. Running\nit does not, by itself, make a dataset HIPAA-compliant, GDPR-compliant, or\ncompliant with any other regime. Whether a masked dataset satisfies a\nregulation as applied to your actual data is a determination for you and\nyour counsel, not a claim this tool makes."],[129,"**It is not a fixed, uneditable bundle.** Every Disguise resolves to plain\npipeline YAML. Nothing stops you from deleting a column entry your data\ndoesn't have, swapping a strategy, or adding columns the template didn't\nanticipate. Treat the output of `decoy templates show` as a draft, not a\nfinal answer."],[127,"**It is not automatic classification.** A Disguise does not scan your data\nand decide which template applies, and it does not apply itself. You choose\na Disguise the same way you choose any other starting template: by name,\nbecause you know your data is HIPAA-shaped or PCI-shaped. This is the same\ndisguises-as-presets stance that shapes STORM (see\nSTORM): the tool surfaces defaults and findings, and\na person decides what to run."],[539,"**Key decisions:**"],[606,"**Mask**: replace real codes with other valid codes from the same corpus"],[141,"**Masking** (`mask:` strategies) is keyed separately, off a `mask_secret_ref`\nyou configure in the pipeline YAML or pass with `--mask-secret`:"],[303,"**Memory error during generation**"],[408,"**Miss identifiers** (false negative): A person name written in lowercase or a specialized location not in the training data may be missed."],[564,"**No conditional generation.** `condition_on` is rejected under DP because joint distributions are not private. All columns are independent."],[563,"**Numeric and categorical only.** Dates, free text, and complex types are generated without DP protection. Declare them as non-DP types."],[78,"**Numeric and categorical only.** Dates, free text, and complex types are not supported under DP; use non-DP generation types for these."],[1019,"**Options**:"],[1029,"**Options**:"],[1051,"**Options**:"],[1077,"**Options**:"],[1093,"**Options**:"],[1099,"**Options**:"],[1116,"**Options**:"],[1134,"**Options**:"],[1149,"**Options**:"],[1165,"**Options**:"],[1177,"**Options**:"],[1198,"**Options**:"],[1226,"**Options**:"],[1243,"**Options**:"],[1282,"**Options**:"],[1319,"**Options**:"],[1335,"**Options**:"],[1356,"**Options**:"],[1366,"**Options**:"],[1384,"**Options**:"],[1401,"**Options**:"],[1420,"**Options**:"],[1441,"**Options**:"],[1470,"**Options**:"],[1493,"**Options**:"],[1503,"**Options**:"],[1522,"**Options**:"],[1545,"**Options**:"],[1552,"**Options**:"],[1565,"**Options**:"],[1583,"**Options**:"],[1597,"**Options**:"],[1614,"**Options**:"],[1629,"**Options**:"],[1654,"**Options**:"],[1682,"**Options**:"],[1712,"**Options**:"],[1741,"*