les a dataset before you write a masking pipeline: what fields\nlook like PII, which columns form a quasi-identifier group together, and a\nre-identification risk score. It never masks anything and never applies a\npipeline on your behalf; it surfaces candidates for you to review. Run\nagainst `decoy` CLI 0.1.0; every command block below is real output."],[161,"STORM scans a dataset before you write a masking pipeline and produces a\nprofile: what's in the data, and where the risk is concentrated."],[766,"STORM's column classifier detects which semantic type a column is likely to\ncontain (SSN, email, a diagnosis code, and so on). It does not mask, redact,\ntransform, or remove any values. A column classified as `ssn` still contains\nSSNs in the clear until a masking step in your pipeline explicitly\ntransforms it."],[169,"STORM's detectors are heuristics: pattern matches, name hints, and\nnamed-entity recognition. They can miss a column that is actually sensitive\n(a false negative) and they can flag a column that isn't (a false positive).\nSTORM does not mask, redact, or transform anything itself, and it does not\napply a pipeline on your behalf. A column the scan flags as `ssn` still\ncontains SSNs in the clear until a masking step in your YAML explicitly\nhandles it."],[443,"STORM's detectors are heuristics. A finding is a candidate, not a verdict:\nyou read it, decide which mask strategy fits, and write that decision into\nthe YAML as an explicit `strategy:` entry. Nothing is masked until you do."],[674,"Strategies"],[30,"Strategies that are deterministic by construction, because they're a pure\nfunction of their input and config: `bucketize`, `redact`, `text_redact`,\n`truncate`, `formula`."],[922,"string"],[938,"string"],[2148,"string"],[2156,"string"],[2160,"string"],[2291,"string"],[2295,"string"],[2313,"string"],[2317,"string"],[2340,"string"],[2362,"string"],[2370,"string"],[2374,"string"],[2397,"string"],[2405,"string"],[2419,"string"],[2423,"string"],[2