ly picking one for you."],[2715,"The NER model to load"],[2753,"The NER model to load"],[2862,"The object path within the bucket."],[2901,"The object path within the bucket."],[757,"The one formal mechanism is `decoy fit --epsilon`: a distribution snapshot's\ncounts are released with per-count noise under differential privacy, exact\nquantiles and means are removed, and min/max collapse to histogram-edge\nresolution. Read that scope narrowly:"],[2667,"The one source column whose value selects the reference row"],[544,"The output is 1,000 rows of synthetic data, generated from the DP snapshot."],[2293,"The period to snap within: `week`, `month`, or `quarter`"],[2881,"The pipeline schema also accepts `type: s3` and `type: gcs` source and\ntarget blocks, shown on their own pages: S3,\nGCS. Both validate with `decoy validate config` and\nboth formats are `csv` or `parquet` only, no fixed-width."],[1956,"The pipeline YAML must declare a `subset:` block (seeds + optional budget /\nedge\\_directions / allow\\_dangling) alongside its `relationships:` block --\nthe same config surface `decoy run` reads. See `decoy schema` for the full\nshape."],[2334,"The pool to map onto"],[758,"The privacy budget is per column histogram. A snapshot of several columns\ncomposes sequentially, so releasing k columns spends roughly `(k + 1) *\nepsilon` of total budget."],[729,"The problem a flat 0/1 contract has"],[248,"The problem: high cardinality"],[2461,"The provider to draw from, for example `person_email`"],[2832,"The reference date the window is measured from"],[2663,"The reference table: a shipped name (for example `us_zip5_city_state`) or `customer:<absolute_path>`"],[1592,"The report is built from the manifest only (evidence-safe). Raw row\nvalues, PII, and STORM profile internals are never included."],[1669,"The run entry must have an evidence\\_path (run with `--evidence-out`)."],[1379,"The run id can be the full UUID or a prefix (at least 4 characters).\nUse `decoy jobs list` to see all run ids."],[143,"The run seed makes output reproducible, but a seed is not a confidentiality\nsecret: it is often stored in the same config file as the rest of the\npipeline. If keyed masking derived its protection from the seed alone, anyone\nwho could read the config could reconstruct the masking. Splitting the two\nmeans the pipeline shape (which columns get which strategy) can be reviewed\nand version-controlled openly, while the thing that actually protects\nre-identification is a secret you hold separately."],[223,"The same value for everyone in a group"],[657,"The seed is not fixed. Check that `global_settings.seed` is set to a constant value:"],[16,"The seed protocol behind reproducible masking and generation."],[2583,"The series generator"],[2177,"The shape of a Decoy pipeline YAML, top to bottom."],[2553,"The single column that partitions rows into groups"],[488,"The sources for every subsetted or related table must be `format: parquet`\n(subsetting does not run on CSV). For the full pipeline shape (sources, tables,\ntargets), see Quickstart."],[751,"The STORM classifier does not de-identify anything"],[456,"The subset block"],[2191,"The tables to mask or generate, and their columns. See Strategies and Providers"],[136,"The unmask model"],[150,"The vault grows with the data it protects, unlike a key or a seed. Treat it\nwith the same handling the source data itself requires."],[147,"The vault is an encrypted file recording each vaulted column's\nsource-to-masked mapping at mask time. Recover originals with:"],[498,"The vault is decrypted under the config's seed, so keep both the config and the\nvault file safe."],[2132,"The vault is encrypted under a key derived from the config's seed. The\nconfig passed to --config must be the SAME config (or at least the same\nglobal\\_settings.seed) used by the `decoy run --vault` call that wrote\nthe vault, otherwise the decrypt will fail and the command exits 1."],[148,"The vault's own encryption key derives from the same `mask_key` as the rest\nof the run, so unlocking the vault requires the mask secret (or, in the\nno-secret fallback, the seed) that produced it. Vault creation is opt-in\ntwice over: a column has to declare `vault: true`, and the operator has to\npass `--vault PATH`. A masking run never writes a vault otherwise."],[1499,"The workspace is a LOCAL convenience area for derived Decoy artifacts\n(scan records, run metadata, evidence manifests, rendered reports). It\ndoes NOT sync with the platform server, track remote state, or replace\nRBAC, audit logs, or managed platform operations."],[538,"Their domain (min/max for numeric, actual categories for categorical)"],[537,"Their type (numeric or categorical)"],[25,"There are two reproducibility scopes, and they answer different questions."],[1411,"There is no `decoy platform` command group. Remote/async job monitoring\nis a platform-service concern, outside this CLI's local-only scope."],[2871,"There is no `endpoint_url` equivalent for GCS: unlike S3, the connector\ndoes not support pointing at a non-Google-hosted GCS-compatible service."],[2923,"There is no `type: sftp` source or target block to write today. This page\nexists so \"does Decoy support SFTP\" has a clear, current answer rather than\nsilence."],[848,"These are `decoy_native`, deterministic and checksummed, so the same input maps to\na valid, stable identifier."],[1410,"This command shows the recorded completed status. It does NOT stream live\nprogress for an in-progress run, because local CLI runs have no background\nmechanism that would allow that."],[633,"This fits a distribution snapshot of the source codes and samples from it. The generated codes match your source frequency (e.g., hypertension codes appear at the same rate as in the original data)."],[302,"This happens with `allow_real_categories: false` (the default). Set `allow_real_categories: true`:"],[170,"This is a deliberate design stance, not a current limitation waiting on a\nfuture release. Decoy does not ship an auto-detect-and-apply pipeline where\nthe tool decides what a column is and masks it without you looking. STORM\nsurfaces candidates; you review them and decide."],[1437,"This is a LOCAL check only. It does NOT check platform server-side\nconditions, engine run-time constraints, data quality, vault access,\nsecrets availability, or network connectivity. Use `decoy validate`\nfor pure schema-only checks; use this command when you want to confirm\nsource files are present before starting a run."],[1520,"This is a read-only command. It does not modify the workspace or\ncontact the platform."],[295,"This is a tradeoff: you protect the most common categories but lose privacy guarantees on rare ones. Use this approach when privacy is a requirement but high-cardinality coverage is not critical."],[427,"This is common with domain-specific or non-standard text. Use a placeholder pass with NER, then add a secondary heuristic pass or manual review. Decoy's NER is intended as a first-line detection aid, not as a guarantee."],[1262,"This is the generated reference for every `decoy` command, kept in sync with the\nCLI itself. Each command group below documents its own arguments and options;\ncommands that only operate on a local `.decoy/` workspace (`project`, `catalog`,\n`jobs`) say so in their own description."],[984,"This is the install path that works right now: clone both repos and install\neach in editable mode into a virtual environment."],[376,"This pulls in spaCy and downloads the `en_core_web_sm` model. The model is \\~50 MB and downloaded once on first use."],[533,"This recipe generates synthetic data with a formal differential privacy guarantee. It walks through configuration, the privacy budget tradeoffs, and how to check the output."],[319,"This recipe masks a single CSV: a synthetic replacement for `email`, a\none-way redaction for `phone`, and a deterministic keyed hash for\n`customer_id` that stays stable across runs. It was run end 